Better Files 1.6.1 by munza (https://github.com/munza/herdr-mods), Apache-2.0.

Changed in this copy:
- views/viewer.js: an Edit mode that edits local text files in place, saves after a short
  pause and asks "Keep mine / Take theirs" when the file changed on disk meanwhile (a file on
  another machine is written there by a script, files/shell.js REMOTE_WRITE); Markdown
  task-list items render as checkboxes that tick the file. The viewer was read-only.
- files/model.js: task-list items as their own preview blocks (TASK, toggleTaskLine).
- actions/open.js: a split viewer records its tab at once (it could fail to claim one).
- main.js: unsaved edits are saved on close; a headless "opener" copy (props mode "opener",
  a floating block in the layout) opens files asked for through
  shared "better-files.open-request" (sent by the open-ref mod) and through a terminal's
  "herdr.open" label (set by the Claude Code mod path-keys, on any machine).
- actions/open.js: an "open" setting (split, default, or tab) for where a file opens; a closed
  viewer pane no longer counts as "already open" while another viewer stays in its tab.
- views/viewer.js: a "Copy text" button on Markdown files copies the file's raw text.
- views/find.js: Cmd-F (better-files.find, bound in keys.json) opens a find bar in a viewer that
  marks matches in the preview, the line view or the editor and steps through them.
- views/rainbow.js: rainbow brackets and rainbow indent in the line view and the preview's code
  blocks, each with a setting (settings.rainbow.brackets / .indent, on by default).
